From: Waltteri Hooli <1420194+wahooli@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: treat LPI MI2S ports as MI2S too

The AYANEO Pocket VERT's speaker amps sit on the LPASS VA domain's MI2S
(LPI_MI2S_RX_0, Android's "MI2S-LPAIF_VA-RX-PRIMARY"), not on one of the
PRIMARY..QUINARY ports. Patches 0060 and 0612/0613 only knew those, so an
LPI port got neither its bit clock at backend startup nor the early port
start the Awinic amps need to see BCLK at DAPM power-up. LPI MI2S already
gets the I2S DAI ops (q6dsp-lpass-ports.c); count it here too, with the
same two ranges.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
@@ -231,6 +231,8 @@
 	switch (cpu_dai->id) {
 	case PRIMARY_MI2S_RX...QUATERNARY_MI2S_TX:
 	case QUINARY_MI2S_RX...QUINARY_MI2S_TX:
+	case LPI_MI2S_RX_0...LPI_MI2S_TX_4:
+	case LPI_MI2S_RX_5...LPI_MI2S_TX_6:
 		if (++pdata->mi2s_clk_count == 1) {
 			ret = clk_prepare_enable(pdata->i2s_clk);
 			if (ret) {
@@ -261,6 +263,8 @@
 	switch (cpu_dai->id) {
 	case PRIMARY_MI2S_RX...QUATERNARY_MI2S_TX:
 	case QUINARY_MI2S_RX...QUINARY_MI2S_TX:
+	case LPI_MI2S_RX_0...LPI_MI2S_TX_4:
+	case LPI_MI2S_RX_5...LPI_MI2S_TX_6:
 		if (--pdata->mi2s_clk_count == 0)
 			clk_disable_unprepare(pdata->i2s_clk);
 		break;
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-lpass-dais.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-lpass-dais.c
@@ -274,7 +274,9 @@
 	if (substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK &&
 	    ((dai->id >= PRIMARY_MI2S_RX && dai->id <= QUATERNARY_MI2S_TX) ||
 	     (dai->id >= QUINARY_MI2S_RX &&
-	      dai->id <= QUINARY_MI2S_TX))) {
+	      dai->id <= QUINARY_MI2S_TX) ||
+	     (dai->id >= LPI_MI2S_RX_0 && dai->id <= LPI_MI2S_TX_4) ||
+	     (dai->id >= LPI_MI2S_RX_5 && dai->id <= LPI_MI2S_TX_6))) {
 		rc = q6apm_graph_start(dai_data->graph[dai->id]);
 		if (rc < 0) {
 			dev_err(dai->dev, "Failed to start APM port %d\n", dai->id);
